# steps/named-struct-exec.md §12: a named Structure's body reads a unit field as a method's body does --
# through the space above it.  Counter\n is 2 after one execution; with g 5, a second execution makes it
# 5 (its declaration runs again).  Was unit_named_struct_stmt_operand_refused ("named Structure body not
# walkable yet: a name that is not a field of this Structure" -- the special path walked the Structure's
# own number fields only).  Entry 7.
size_t: g 2U
Counter:
    size_t: n 0U
    n: n + g
return
Counter
size_t: a 9U
a: Counter\n
g: 5U
Counter
int: ok 0
if: a = 2U && Counter\n = 5U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
